{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1788819939","published":"2026-09-07T22:25:50Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:30:06.887528465Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-58016"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-58016","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: Out-of-bounds read in the D-Bus introspection XML parser\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-58016.patch: fix the inverted <node> nesting\n       check in parser_start_element() in gio/gdbusintrospection.c, which\n       accepted a <node> element inside <method>/<signal>/<property>/<arg>\n       and left the parser reading X->pdata[X->len - 1] with len == 0\n     - CVE-2026-58016\n   * debian/rules: add arm to the qemu-buildd architecture list, raising\n     test_timeout_multiplier from 5 to 20 on armel. Debian builds armel on real\n     ARM hardware and so left it in the \"slow architecture\" tier, but this\n     platform builds it under emulation, where the +slow suite exceeds the\n     resulting 900s cap non-deterministically (gvariant 435s/262s/timeout,\n     642026 488s/501s/timeout across three runs of the same tree). No test is\n     skipped and no other architecture is affected: arm64 and amd64 do not\n     match the arm filter word.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libglib2.0-0","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libglib2.0-0?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.66.8-1+deb11u8+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1788819939.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libglib2.0-bin","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libglib2.0-bin?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.66.8-1+deb11u8+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1788819939.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libglib2.0-data","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","pu